1)After viewing Zomato.com in Chrome DevTools on iPhone 12, iPad, and Desktop, these UI/layout changes can be observed:

  Navigation and Search Bar:
  On desktop, the navigation menu and search bar are displayed horizontally with more space. On iPhone 12, the layout becomes compact, and some navigation options may be hidden or rearranged. iPad shows an intermediate tablet-style layout.
  Content Layout:
  Desktop displays restaurant cards and other content in multiple columns. On iPhone 12, the content is mostly shown in a single-column vertical layout for easier scrolling. iPad usually displays fewer columns than desktop but more than mobile.
  Images and Text Size:
  On mobile, images, buttons, and text are resized to fit the smaller screen, with touch-friendly spacing. On desktop, images are larger and more content can be displayed side by side, while iPad provides a balanced layout between mobile and desktop.
